Return a narrow splitter width for the Dolphin status bar

Dolphin 26.08 derives the geometry of its small status bar from the style
in src/statusbar/dolphinstatusbar.cpp. The status bar reads
PM_SplitterWidth. It computes a clipping amount of 2 + 2 times that value.
The layout margins consume three clipping amounts. The width budget
reserves the text width, two clipping amounts, and one average character
width. The label therefore loses one clipping amount minus one average
character width. Breeze returns 1 pixel, so the label keeps a small
reserve. QtCurve returns 7 pixels by default, or 6 for the other splitter
line styles. The label then loses up to 9 pixels and Dolphin elides its
text. For example "1 folder, 5 files (1.1 MiB)" turns into
"1 folder, 5…s (1.1 MiB)". The clipping amount also sets the minimum
height of the bar. The bar sheds that surplus and matches the Breeze
geometry. Return the Breeze value for the Dolphin status bar. Splitter
handles and dock separators keep their own width.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
index cb030b41..bd090e25 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
@@ -1685,8 +1685,15 @@ Style::pixelMetric(PixelMetric metric, const QStyleOption *option,
         return 4;
     // case PM_DockWindowHandleExtent:
     //     return 10;
-    case PM_DockWidgetSeparatorExtent:
     case PM_SplitterWidth:
+        // Dolphin subtracts this metric from the width that it leaves for
+        // the label in its small status bar. A wide handle makes Dolphin
+        // elide that label. Only the Dolphin status bar sees the narrow
+        // Breeze value.
+        if (qtcCheckType(widget, "DolphinStatusBar"))
+            return 1;
+        QTC_FALLTHROUGH();
+    case PM_DockWidgetSeparatorExtent:
         return LINE_1DOT==opts.splitters ? 7 : 6;
     case PM_ToolBarHandleExtent:
         return LINE_1DOT==opts.handles ? 7 : 8;
